{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Forward node2 inventory log messages to node1 and persist them at /var/log/inventory/node2.log.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A tagged inventory message was received in the required file before restarts, while a non-inventory control message was excluded. Final evidence shows all three inventory test messages retained, correct source identity, an active TCP connection, and no negative-control messages.","evidence_ids":["cmd-82f2c7a8dfa94cf3","cmd-6590d096fdba4d36","cmd-f61f8f7f8771473e"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Keep collection, stored data, and fresh log delivery working after node1 restarts.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 had a healthy pre-restart collector, acknowledged a scheduled reboot, changed boot ID, recovered its rsyslog listener and firewall rule, retained existing data, and then received a fresh inventory message from node2.","evidence_ids":["cmd-922667c43d6c4a08","cmd-cc20a36ef4974fc9","cmd-d5248653da7640da","cmd-75db9d40b1034980","cmd-9a5befd1f2f74447","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep forwarding and end-to-end log delivery working after node2 restarts.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 had a healthy enabled forwarder before restart, acknowledged a scheduled reboot, changed boot ID, recovered rsyslog and its established TCP session, and sent a fresh inventory message that node1 persisted while retaining earlier messages.","evidence_ids":["cmd-32e3a8bf937748b1","cmd-33aea07e2b6d475f","cmd-19d48619683c4a9f","cmd-08089b58ec134ff1","cmd-f61f8f7f8771473e","global:before_prepare:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64. The existing EL10 rsyslog package was used, configurations validated successfully, and package-health observations remained healthy.","evidence_ids":["cmd-50045372257b4036","cmd-0b75c1b2ccbb4a69","cmd-08fbe3510bd24d44","cmd-f61f8f7f8771473e","cmd-4e276f3b2d78490f","cmd-9bf331f1d2f14f00","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The configuration files, log directory, narrow source-restricted firewall rule, service restarts, synthetic test messages, and mandatory node restarts all had clear implementation or bounded-verification roles. Transient reboot units left no residue; both nodes ended with no failed units or rsyslog warnings, healthy package state, and only the required new collector listener on node1.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ff0e792719c54f17","cmd-146565702c5d4b81","cmd-2778510103fc4fba","cmd-4e276f3b2d78490f","cmd-9bf331f1d2f14f00","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. Direct end-to-end tests demonstrate filtered persistence before restarts and fresh delivery after separate restarts of both managed nodes. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for both nodes and independently corroborated by lifecycle boot identities. Platform versions and system health were preserved.","limitations":["End-to-end behavior was exercised with logger-generated messages carrying the inventory program tag because discovery found no running inventory unit or process; no message emitted by an actual inventory application process was captured.","The node2 disk queue was configured and survived restart, but delivery of a message deliberately queued during collector downtime was not separately exercised; this does not undermine the directly demonstrated requirement that fresh flow works after either restart."]}
